 "findings": [
  {
   "heading": "By summary statistic of another column / Pela estatística de resumo de outra coluna",
   "segment_index": "S18.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/factors.qmd:277-277",
   "tr_span": "chapters/factors.pt.qmd:249-249",
   "proposition": "The English says the levels of delay_cat are ordered by ascending MEDIAN CT value of each group, matching fct_reorder(delay_cat, ct_blood, \"median\"); the Portuguese says the order reflects 'os valores medios de CT crescentes de cada valor de CT medio dos grupos', i.e. the ascending MEAN CT value.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Portuguese reader concludes that fct_reorder() with \"median\" sorts groups by their mean, and will expect a different bar order than the code produces, or will pass \"mean\" believing it is equivalent. The same paragraph two sentences earlier used 'mediano' correctly, so the reader has no cue that one of the two is a slip.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "In plots / Em graficos",
   "segment_index": "S26.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/factors.qmd:449-449",
   "tr_span": "chapters/factors.pt.qmd:402-402",
   "proposition": "The English states that levels displayed via x =, color = or size = are handled by passing drop = FALSE to the CORRESPONDING scale_ function (scale_color_discrete() for color =, scale_size_discrete() for size =). The Portuguese makes 'x =' the condition and color =/size = the thing supplied: 'Se seus niveis sao exibidos com x = (para o eixo x), voce deve fornecer color = ou size = para a funcao scale_color_discrete() ou para scale_size_discrete()'.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Portuguese reader whose factor levels are on the x-axis is told to supply color = or size = to scale_color_discrete() or scale_size_discrete(). Following that gives no drop = FALSE on the x scale, so unused levels are still dropped from the axis and the reader cannot get the standardised axis the section promises.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Reduce into \"Other\" / Reduzir para \"Outro\"",
   "segment_index": "S23.P1",
   "kind": "added",
   "en_span": "chapters/factors.qmd:403-403",
   "tr_span": "chapters/factors.pt.qmd:361-361",
   "proposition": "The Portuguese sentence carries the source English clause 'aside from \"Port Hospital\" and \"Central Hospital\", are combined into \"Other\".' inline, immediately followed by its Portuguese rendering, so the same statement is present twice in one sentence; the English original states it once.",
   "reader_consequence": "A Portuguese reader meets an untranslated English clause spliced into the middle of a Portuguese sentence, with a full stop inside it. The sentence has two verbs for one subject and reads as corrupt, so the reader cannot tell whether the English clause is a quotation, a leftover, or a separate rule about fct_other().",
   "confidence": "high"
  }
 ]
